Appendix G: Exergy Balance Closure and Layer 0 Validation

G.1 The Shukuya Exergy Balance

The general form of the exergy balance equation for a human body as a thermodynamic system is:

[\text{exergy input}] - [\text{exergy consumption}] = [\text{exergy stored}] + [\text{exergy output}]

Exergy input consists of five components:

1. Warm exergy generated by metabolism
2. Warm/cool and wet/dry exergies of the inhaled humid air
3. Warm and wet exergies of the liquid water generated in the core by metabolism
4. Warm/cool and wet/dry exergies of the sum of liquid water generated in the shell by metabolism and dry air to let the liquid water disperse
5. Warm/cool radiant exergy absorbed by the whole skin and clothing surfaces

Exergy output consists of four components:

1. Warm and wet exergy contained in the exhaled humid air
2. Warm/cool and wet/dry exergy contained in resultant humid air containing the evaporated sweat
3. Warm/cool radiant exergy discharged from the whole skin and clothing surfaces
4. Warm/cool exergy transferred by convection from the whole skin and clothing surfaces into surrounding air

G.2 Mathematical Form of Individual Terms

Warm/cool exergy (sensible heat transfer):

\dot{X}_Q^{wc} = \dot{Q} \left( 1 - \frac{T_0}{T} \right)

where T is absolute temperature, T_0 is the dead-state temperature, and \dot{Q} is positive for heat flow into the system.

Wet/dry exergy of water vapor:

\dot{X}_v^{wd} = \dot{m}_v R_v T_0 \ln\left( \frac{P_v}{P_{v,0}} \right)

where \dot{m}_v is the vapor mass flow, R_v is the specific gas constant of water vapor, P_v is the vapor partial pressure, and P_{v,0} = \phi_0 P_{\text{sat}}(T_0) is the dead-state vapor pressure.

Liquid water exergy:

\dot{X}_{\text{liq}}^{wd} = \dot{m}_{\text{liq}} \left[ (h(T_s) - h(T_0)) - T_0 (s(T_s) - s(T_0)) + v_{\text{liq}} (P_s - P_0) \right]

where h and s are specific enthalpy and entropy from the IAPWS-95 formulation for water.

Radiative exergy (gray-surface approximation):

\dot{X}_{\text{rad}} = \varepsilon \sigma A (T_s^4 - T_r^4) \left( 1 - \frac{T_0}{T_r} \right)

where T_s is surface temperature, T_r is effective radiative temperature, \varepsilon is emissivity, and \sigma is the Stefan–Boltzmann constant.

G.3 Layer 0 Closure Criterion

Closure is evaluated as:

\frac{\left| \sum \dot{X}_{\text{in}} - \sum \dot{X}_{\text{out}} - \dot{X}_D - \frac{dX_B}{dt} \right|}{\max_j |\text{term}_j|} \le 1\%

evaluated on a scenario-per-term basis, with a per-term uncertainty budget. Partial cancellation between large in/out terms can fake closure; the normalization prevents this.

G.4 Decomposition of \dot{X}_{D,\text{body}}

The body exergy destruction decomposes into:

\dot{X}_{D,\text{body}} = \dot{X}_{D,\text{met}} + \dot{X}_{D,\text{transfer}}

where \dot{X}_{D,\text{met}} is the metabolic irreversibility (dominant, approximately 90% of total, and essentially independent of control actions) and \dot{X}_{D,\text{transfer}} is the irreversible degradation at skin/clothing/environment interfaces.

Only \dot{X}_{D,\text{transfer}} belongs in the objective. Minimizing \dot{X}_{D,\text{met}} is a constant offset that adds noise to the optimization.

