Appendix H: Benchmark Statistical Protocol

H.1 Architectures

Architecture Physiology Modes Objective Hardware
A Simple comfort Convection only Energy Standard HVAC
B Physiological Radiation only Energy Radiant panels
C Physiological Radiant + convective Energy Hybrid
D Physiological All feasible Energy Full actuator set
E (baseline) Population model All feasible Exergy Full actuator set
F (TS-Engine) Physiological state feedback All feasible Exergy Pareto Full actuator set
G (oracle) Perfect physiological state All feasible Exergy Pareto Full actuator set

H.2 Scenarios

1. Hot-dry: high T_a, low humidity
2. Hot-humid: high T_a, high humidity
3. Mixed: moderate temperature and humidity
4. Cold: low T_a
5. Grid outage: limited electricity
6. Water scarcity: limited water
7. High solar gain: strong radiative load
8. High internal gain: dense occupancy

H.3 Metrics

· J_{\text{ex}}: integrated exergy cost (system + transfer)
· W_{\text{water}}: water consumption
· D_{\text{discomfort}}: discomfort penalty
· E_{\text{el}}: electrical energy
· \eta_{\text{MPC}}: optimization regret (or gap to best-known)
· Switching frequency
· Pareto hypervolume
· \varepsilon-indicator (additive)

H.4 Falsification Criterion for H₃

H₃ is falsified if:

\forall s \in \mathcal{S}, \; \mathcal{P}_F(s) \not\prec \mathcal{P}_E(s)

where \prec denotes strict Pareto dominance of fronts and \mathcal{P}_E is the Pareto front of Architecture E at equal discomfort and equal resource constraints.

H.5 Statistical Testing

Run \ge 10 seeds/weather realizations per scenario. Compute hypervolume difference against a fixed reference point. Report 95% confidence intervals. Require a minimum-effect threshold of 5% hypervolume improvement for a "dominance" claim in a given scenario.

Hypervolume indicator. For a front \mathcal{P} with reference point r:

\mathcal{H}(\mathcal{P}, r) = \Lambda\left( \bigcup_{p \in \mathcal{P}} [r, p] \right)

where \Lambda is the Lebesgue measure and [r, p] is the hyperrectangle bounded by r and p. F dominates E in hypervolume if \mathcal{H}(\mathcal{P}_F, r) > \mathcal{H}(\mathcal{P}_E, r).

Additive \varepsilon-indicator. The minimum \varepsilon such that for every p_E \in \mathcal{P}_E, there exists p_F \in \mathcal{P}_F with p_F + \varepsilon \mathbf{1} \succeq p_E.

